        "_raw_text": "{\"weakness\":\"Warm batch latency is now ~45.8ms with cold ~45.9ms, so nearly all remaining time is fixed per-query work; no stage breakdown exists to show whether corpus normalization, hashing, or result assembly dominates, and RSS rose from 22016KB to 24588KB after the index change.\",\"hypothesis\":\"A large share of the remaining ~45.8ms batch time is repeated per-query corpus normalization/tokenization work; reusing one hash-keyed parsed corpus per batch, guarded by corpus_sha256, should cut median and p95 batch latency by at least 20% without changing any per-query sha256 or counts.\",\"metric\":\"median_batch_ms, p95_batch_ms, cold_batch_ms, rss_kb from the schema-1 benchmark; gate on correctness 1.0, zero failed_queries, and identical per-query sha256/count for all 20 queries versus corpus_sha256 37c5a6ee...\",\"change\":\"Add stage timers around corpus load/normalize/score/assemble, then reuse a single parsed corpus per batch keyed by corpus_sha256, falling back to fresh parse on hash mismatch; keep result ordering and output bytes unchanged.\",\"risk\":\"Cache keyed incorrectly or reused after mid-batch corpus mutation could return stale or wrong results, and retained parsed state could grow RSS further; mitigate by strict corpus_sha256 keying, hash-mismatch invalidation, and per-query sha256 equality checks.\",\"reversible\":true,\"expected_files\":[\"search/index.py\",\"search/query.py\",\"benchmarks/bench_search.py\",\"tests/test_search_correctness.py\"]}",
        "change": "Add stage timers around corpus load/normalize/score/assemble, then reuse a single parsed corpus per batch keyed by corpus_sha256, falling back to fresh parse on hash mismatch; keep result ordering and output bytes unchanged.",
        "expected_files": [
          "search/index.py",
          "search/query.py",
          "benchmarks/bench_search.py",
          "tests/test_search_correctness.py"
        ],
        "hypothesis": "A large share of the remaining ~45.8ms batch time is repeated per-query corpus normalization/tokenization work; reusing one hash-keyed parsed corpus per batch, guarded by corpus_sha256, should cut median and p95 batch latency by at least 20% without changing any per-query sha256 or counts.",
        "metric": "median_batch_ms, p95_batch_ms, cold_batch_ms, rss_kb from the schema-1 benchmark; gate on correctness 1.0, zero failed_queries, and identical per-query sha256/count for all 20 queries versus corpus_sha256 37c5a6ee...",
